      },
      "call": "session.prompt",
      "id": "session.prompt",
      "note": "Realistic SDK input union: `tools` is a name->bool map, `snapshotInitialization` is \"wait\", and the text part carries the SDK's extra synthetic/time fields; the compat layer accepts all of it (the scaffold DTO would have rejected the body). The RESPONSE still diverges: daemon {info:{sessionID,messageID,role,createdMs,providerID,modelID}, parts:[{type,text}]} vs SDK AssistantMessage id/time{}/parentID/mode/agent/path/cost/tokens and Part id/sessionID/messageID.",
      "request": {
        "body": "{\"model\":{\"modelID\":\"m\",\"providerID\":\"fake\"},\"parts\":[{\"synthetic\":false,\"text\":\"ping\",\"time\":{\"start\":0},\"type\":\"text\"}],\"snapshotInitialization\":\"wait\",\"tools\":{\"read_file\":true,\"write_file\":false}}",
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/session/@string/message",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "info": {
            "createdMs": "@int",
            "messageID": "@string",
            "modelID": "m",
            "providerID": "fake",
            "role": "assistant",
            "sessionID": "@string"
          },
          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "pong",
              "type": "text"
            }
